1
00:00:47,964 --> 00:00:49,174
Huh? Wait.

2
00:00:49,758 --> 00:00:51,384
Hey, why is your cannon here?

3
00:00:51,468 --> 00:00:53,011
What are you talking about?

4
00:00:53,094 --> 00:00:54,846
It's been here all along.

5
00:00:54,929 --> 00:00:56,806
Come on.
Do you think I'm blind?

6
00:00:56,890 --> 00:00:58,725
When did you move it
while I wasn't looking?

7
00:00:58,808 --> 00:01:01,186
Come on, man.
You have to act like it isn't here!

8
00:01:01,269 --> 00:01:04,022
Y-yes, s-sir, driver.

9
00:01:04,105 --> 00:01:05,815
You've been watching the whole time,
so tell me.

10
00:01:06,733 --> 00:01:07,776
It wasn't here, was it?

11
00:01:15,533 --> 00:01:16,951
Well...

12
00:01:17,035 --> 00:01:19,871
Well, regardless of who wins...

13
00:01:19,954 --> 00:01:23,374
I'd like to treat you to a glass
of makgeolli for this round.

14
00:01:24,375 --> 00:01:25,376
Please, have some!

15
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:26,628
Thank you.

16
00:01:26,711 --> 00:01:28,671
Oh, don't mention it!

17
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:33,134
- I'll enjoy this, okay?
- Yes, yes, sir.

18
00:01:33,218 --> 00:01:35,428
Have as much as you like! Yes, yes.

19
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:53,738
Could you take me to Pyeongtaek?

20
00:01:57,158 --> 00:01:58,034
Sometimes, like this,

21
00:01:58,118 --> 00:02:00,620
I pick up passengers
without a reservation.

22
00:02:01,246 --> 00:02:03,623
Meeting someone unexpectedly

23
00:02:03,706 --> 00:02:05,458
is one of the joys of driving a taxi.

24
00:02:05,542 --> 00:02:06,835
All right.

25
00:02:20,265 --> 00:02:22,058
Did you want to tell me something?

26
00:02:27,272 --> 00:02:29,566
There are two rules in this taxi.

27
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:33,778
Sometimes, like now,
I pick up new passengers.

28
00:02:33,862 --> 00:02:37,699
But most of my passengers
are regulars with reservations.

29
00:02:37,782 --> 00:02:39,742
On the way to your destination,

30
00:02:39,826 --> 00:02:42,829
I play music
that my passengers want to hear.

31
00:02:46,457 --> 00:02:49,627
Is there a song you'd like to hear?

32
00:02:52,839 --> 00:02:54,132
Yes.

33
00:02:54,215 --> 00:02:56,634
You can just tell me now,

34
00:02:56,718 --> 00:02:58,011
or you can use the

35
00:02:58,094 --> 00:03:00,555
notepad back there and write it down.

36
00:03:00,638 --> 00:03:01,472
All right.

37
00:03:01,556 --> 00:03:04,183
If I don't have the CD or tape in the car,

38
00:03:04,267 --> 00:03:06,603
I can connect your phone, too.

39
00:03:06,686 --> 00:03:08,021
I see.

40
00:03:08,104 --> 00:03:10,773
I always wonder what song
my passengers will request.

41
00:03:10,857 --> 00:03:14,402
That's what I look forward to most.

42
00:03:15,194 --> 00:03:17,530
It'll probably take about an hour.

43
00:03:19,324 --> 00:03:21,784
You're a very thoughtful person.

44
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:23,494
Yes.

45
00:03:25,330 --> 00:03:26,164
Yes.

46
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:27,874
Understood.

47
00:03:56,653 --> 00:03:58,404
Sir, we've arrived.

48
00:03:58,488 --> 00:03:59,697
Yes.

49
00:03:59,781 --> 00:04:02,450
Driver, could you wait here
for a little while?

50
00:04:02,533 --> 00:04:04,994
Something came up, and I have to go
to Jeonju right away.

51
00:04:05,078 --> 00:04:07,747
That's quite a ways away.

52
00:04:07,830 --> 00:04:09,332
Sure. Go ahead. I'll wait.

53
00:04:09,415 --> 00:04:10,875
Thank you.

54
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:44,951
You didn't bail on me, did you?

55
00:04:48,621 --> 00:04:50,498
There he is.

56
00:04:50,581 --> 00:04:51,416
Yes.

57
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,127
- You're back?
- Yes. Have you been waiting long?

58
00:04:54,210 --> 00:04:55,086
Let's get going.

59
00:04:55,169 --> 00:04:56,087
- Yes.
- Yes.

60
00:05:15,606 --> 00:05:16,691
By any chance...

61
00:05:16,774 --> 00:05:19,193
You're not going to Jeonju
to buy bread, are you?

62
00:05:19,861 --> 00:05:20,695
Pardon?

63
00:05:22,071 --> 00:05:24,157
I noticed the paper bag you're carrying...

64
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:26,409
and wondered if you liked bread.

65
00:05:27,118 --> 00:05:28,244
This?

66
00:05:30,371 --> 00:05:33,082
When you think of Jeonju and
Korea's three top bakeries...

67
00:05:33,166 --> 00:05:35,335
there's PNB Poongnyeon Bakery.

68
00:05:35,418 --> 00:05:36,252
Is that so?

69
00:05:36,335 --> 00:05:38,046
So you haven't tried it.

70
00:05:38,129 --> 00:05:39,464
No.

71
00:05:39,547 --> 00:05:41,674
They're famous for
their Choco Pies.

72
00:05:41,758 --> 00:05:43,509
They're too sweet for me.

73
00:05:43,593 --> 00:05:46,262
I can't eat more than
four of them.

74
00:05:47,055 --> 00:05:49,766
Of course, if you eat more than
four Choco Pies...

75
00:05:52,060 --> 00:05:54,479
Well, since you're going to Jeonju,
you should stop by.

76
00:05:54,562 --> 00:05:56,439
They have plenty besides Choco Pies.

77
00:05:57,106 --> 00:05:59,067
Is it really that famous?

78
00:06:00,359 --> 00:06:01,903
Is it really that famous?

79
00:06:01,986 --> 00:06:03,404
Sir...

80
00:06:03,488 --> 00:06:06,115
You really haven't tried PNB.

81
00:06:06,199 --> 00:06:08,659
That's insane.
Seriously, that's a problem.

82
00:06:08,743 --> 00:06:10,411
How good can it possibly be

83
00:06:10,495 --> 00:06:13,289
that you'd take a taxi all the
way to Jeonju to buy Choco Pies?

84
00:06:13,372 --> 00:06:14,582
Come on, sir.

85
00:06:14,665 --> 00:06:17,502
I usually can't even finish a slice
of bread, you know?

86
00:06:17,585 --> 00:06:19,796
But their Choco Pies...

87
00:06:19,879 --> 00:06:22,882
I can eat three in one sitting,
not just two.

88
00:06:22,965 --> 00:06:26,302
They're in a whole different league
from the Choco Pies at the grocery store.

89
00:06:26,385 --> 00:06:28,596
You really should try them, sir.

90
00:06:28,679 --> 00:06:29,931
This is so frustrating.

91
00:06:38,231 --> 00:06:39,607
That's right.

92
00:06:39,690 --> 00:06:41,400
This place only takes cash?

93
00:06:41,984 --> 00:06:43,194
Where can I get cash?

94
00:06:43,778 --> 00:06:45,571
Should we look for an ATM nearby?

95
00:06:45,655 --> 00:06:48,783
The line's probably only
going to get longer.

96
00:06:50,576 --> 00:06:51,953
Sir.

97
00:06:52,036 --> 00:06:53,496
I'm really sorry to ask, but...

98
00:06:53,579 --> 00:06:57,250
Since you'll have to
wait here for me anyway,

99
00:06:57,875 --> 00:07:00,294
could you hold my place in line?

100
00:07:00,378 --> 00:07:02,255
I'll buy you some Choco Pies too.

101
00:07:02,338 --> 00:07:03,339
Please.

102
00:07:06,342 --> 00:07:07,510
Sure.

103
00:07:07,593 --> 00:07:08,427
All right, that'll work.

104
00:07:08,511 --> 00:07:10,221
Thank you, sir!

105
00:07:10,304 --> 00:07:11,431
What a relief.

106
00:07:26,028 --> 00:07:28,364
'Open'

107
00:07:31,284 --> 00:07:32,910
Come on in.

108
00:07:40,126 --> 00:07:41,419
Just a moment.

109
00:07:43,337 --> 00:07:44,380
Come on in.

110
00:07:45,047 --> 00:07:47,216
Just a moment, please.

111
00:07:50,386 --> 00:07:51,888
Come on in.

112
00:07:51,971 --> 00:07:53,181
Just a moment.

113
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:57,185
Come on in.

114
00:07:57,977 --> 00:07:59,061
Just a moment.

115
00:08:03,608 --> 00:08:04,442
Come on in.

116
00:08:05,359 --> 00:08:06,986
- Let's hurry up and get inside.
- Come on in.

117
00:08:07,069 --> 00:08:07,987
Yes.

118
00:08:21,167 --> 00:08:22,835
Oh, sir.

119
00:08:22,919 --> 00:08:24,962
What good is this little bit going to do?

120
00:08:25,838 --> 00:08:27,340
How are you going to manage
if you're this timid?

121
00:08:27,423 --> 00:08:28,799
Come on, raise it a little!

122
00:08:28,883 --> 00:08:30,134
Yes, all right.

123
00:08:30,218 --> 00:08:31,594
- Yes...
- This one too, huh?

124
00:08:31,677 --> 00:08:33,179
Your kid will likes this one too.

125
00:08:33,262 --> 00:08:34,096
Thank you.

126
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:39,894
She never showed up.

127
00:08:41,145 --> 00:08:42,355
She skipped out on the fare.

128
00:08:42,438 --> 00:08:45,775
Was that her scheme to get to
Jeonju without paying the fare?

129
00:08:47,068 --> 00:08:48,986
What a horrible woman.

130
00:08:49,070 --> 00:08:50,613
When I got to the register,

131
00:08:50,696 --> 00:08:52,406
I found out I could transfer money, too.

132
00:08:52,490 --> 00:08:55,076
So she didn't actually
need to withdraw cash.

133
00:08:55,159 --> 00:08:57,370
That cold-hearted woman.

134
00:08:57,453 --> 00:08:59,830
She was my first fare that day,
so I didn't have her number.

135
00:09:00,414 --> 00:09:03,209
Still, I wondered if something
might have happened to her,

136
00:09:03,292 --> 00:09:05,086
so I waited a little longer.

137
00:09:06,546 --> 00:09:08,005
On the way down to Jeonju,

138
00:09:08,089 --> 00:09:11,008
I thought of the song she'd requested.

139
00:09:11,092 --> 00:09:13,344
I didn't understand what
the song meant back then.

140
00:09:15,763 --> 00:09:19,350
♪ You said you'd come back ♪

141
00:09:21,227 --> 00:09:25,022
♪ You said it would only
take a little while ♪

142
00:09:26,691 --> 00:09:30,444
♪ You told me to wait here ♪

143
00:09:30,528 --> 00:09:32,113
♪ You lied ♪

144
00:09:32,196 --> 00:09:34,699
♪ You lied, you lied ♪

145
00:09:37,493 --> 00:09:41,205
♪ I stood there staring
as the sun went down ♪

146
00:09:42,999 --> 00:09:46,002
♪ I huddled there as the night wore on ♪

147
00:09:48,337 --> 00:09:52,091
♪ In the end, you never showed up ♪

148
00:09:52,174 --> 00:09:57,138
♪ You lied, you lied ♪

149
00:09:57,722 --> 00:10:02,518
♪ Only you ♪

150
00:10:03,811 --> 00:10:07,440
♪ I waited for you endlessly ♪

151
00:10:08,566 --> 00:10:13,487
♪ Your words ♪

152
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:19,410
♪ I believed every word you said ♪

153
00:10:25,666 --> 00:10:30,254
♪ The road froze in the bitter wind ♪

154
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:40,681
♪ I froze, white as snow ♪

155
00:11:23,849 --> 00:11:25,017
Excuse me, sir.

156
00:11:25,101 --> 00:11:26,769
I'm heading back to Seoul anyway.

157
00:11:26,852 --> 00:11:29,480
If you can wait a little longer,
would you like to ride back with me?

158
00:11:30,564 --> 00:11:32,358
Well, sure.

159
00:11:32,441 --> 00:11:35,736
That's better than driving back empty.

160
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:36,737
Thank you.

161
00:11:38,197 --> 00:11:39,824
For all you coffee lovers,

162
00:11:39,907 --> 00:11:42,243
this should be welcome news.

163
00:11:42,326 --> 00:11:44,912
According to a study
published by a research team,

164
00:11:44,995 --> 00:11:48,040
people who drink three or
four cups of coffee a day

165
00:11:48,124 --> 00:11:50,126
were followed over the long term.

166
00:11:50,209 --> 00:11:51,794
Their risk of diabetes, heart disease,

167
00:11:51,877 --> 00:11:55,339
and Parkinson's disease
was found to be lower.

168
00:11:55,423 --> 00:11:56,590
Another research team

169
00:11:56,674 --> 00:11:59,635
studied 500,000 people
in the UK and found that

170
00:11:59,718 --> 00:12:02,388
people who drink coffee
every day live longer...

171
00:12:06,976 --> 00:12:08,811
Thank you so much.

172
00:12:09,395 --> 00:12:10,604
Here, sir. Have a cup of this.

173
00:12:12,773 --> 00:12:14,942
Nice of you.

174
00:12:15,025 --> 00:12:17,570
I was just craving a coffee.

175
00:12:17,653 --> 00:12:19,238
Thanks. I'll enjoy it.

176
00:12:19,321 --> 00:12:21,115
Thanks for waiting.

177
00:12:21,198 --> 00:12:22,575
The meter's been running, after all.

178
00:12:22,658 --> 00:12:23,868
I should be thanking you.

179
00:12:26,912 --> 00:12:28,247
All right, let's get going.

180
00:12:28,330 --> 00:12:30,416
Sir, before we go...

181
00:12:30,499 --> 00:12:31,542
Sorry to keep asking,

182
00:12:31,625 --> 00:12:35,212
could we stop at a
nearby ATM one more time?

183
00:12:35,296 --> 00:12:37,965
I need to withdraw a little more cash.

184
00:12:39,216 --> 00:12:42,136
In billiards,
the final stop is always three-cushion.

185
00:12:42,219 --> 00:12:44,388
You have to hit three spots to finish.

186
00:12:44,472 --> 00:12:48,100
There's an ATM nearby that I know.

187
00:12:48,184 --> 00:12:50,269
That day,
while I was looking for that woman,

188
00:12:50,352 --> 00:12:54,106
I checked every ATM near
PNB Pungnyeon Bakery.

189
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:57,651
So this must be near the
famous PNB Pungnyeon Bakery?

190
00:12:57,735 --> 00:12:59,236
Yes.

191
00:13:11,373 --> 00:13:13,167
If you drink coffee often,

192
00:13:13,250 --> 00:13:15,294
you may want to keep this in mind.

193
00:13:15,377 --> 00:13:18,380
According to one research team,
drinking large amounts of coffee

194
00:13:18,464 --> 00:13:21,175
can increase the risk of heart arrhythmia

195
00:13:21,258 --> 00:13:23,761
and worsen anxiety symptoms.

196
00:13:23,844 --> 00:13:25,387
The team published its findings.

197
00:13:25,971 --> 00:13:28,974
The team also said caffeine,
a component of coffee,

198
00:13:29,058 --> 00:13:31,852
- can interfere with calcium and iron absorption...
- So are we supposed to drink it or not?

199
00:13:31,936 --> 00:13:34,772
People with osteoporosis or anemia

200
00:13:34,855 --> 00:13:36,106
should take particular care.

201
00:13:36,190 --> 00:13:37,316
urged...

202
00:13:44,990 --> 00:13:47,451
Phishing crimes are on the rise.

203
00:13:47,535 --> 00:13:49,453
Yesterday, thanks to a taxi
driver's quick thinking,

204
00:13:49,537 --> 00:13:52,915
a cash courier for a
phone scam was arrested.

205
00:13:52,998 --> 00:13:54,375
Let's hear what happened

206
00:13:54,458 --> 00:13:57,086
from the taxi driver's own account.

207
00:13:57,753 --> 00:13:59,171
As soon as we got to Yeoju,

208
00:13:59,255 --> 00:14:01,173
he asked me to wait a little.

209
00:14:01,257 --> 00:14:04,969
Then he went to an ATM and took
a long time before coming back.

210
00:14:05,052 --> 00:14:07,429
Then he asked to go to Paju.

211
00:14:07,513 --> 00:14:11,267
He got in carrying what
looked like a shopping bag.

212
00:14:11,350 --> 00:14:15,020
The whole way,
he was making calls and texting.

213
00:14:15,104 --> 00:14:16,188
That's when

214
00:14:16,772 --> 00:14:20,568
I realized, 'This is a phone scam.'

215
00:14:20,651 --> 00:14:22,194
From then on, I just kept driving.

216
00:14:22,778 --> 00:14:25,072
Could you wait here for a moment, sir?

217
00:14:25,155 --> 00:14:27,199
I need to go down to Jeonju right away.

218
00:14:27,283 --> 00:14:28,617
Sorry to keep you waiting.

219
00:14:28,701 --> 00:14:29,910
Let's get going.

220
00:14:39,169 --> 00:14:42,965
Could we stop by one
more ATM before we go?

221
00:14:57,855 --> 00:14:59,356
This is the 112 emergency dispatch center.

222
00:15:02,192 --> 00:15:04,069
Let's go, sir.

223
00:15:05,321 --> 00:15:06,488
Go ahead.

224
00:15:06,572 --> 00:15:07,531
Yes.

225
00:15:22,796 --> 00:15:24,006
Are you the caller?

226
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:26,508
It's Dad.

227
00:15:29,803 --> 00:15:31,347
My father passed away last year...

228
00:15:31,430 --> 00:15:33,641
I know, yeah...

229
00:15:33,724 --> 00:15:37,603
I called because I'm not home
and thought you might worry.

230
00:15:37,686 --> 00:15:40,439
I brought a passenger down to Jeonju.

231
00:15:44,193 --> 00:15:46,946
Are you in an emergency?

232
00:15:47,863 --> 00:15:49,156
Of course.

233
00:15:50,324 --> 00:15:53,285
Don't you know everyone's lining up
to ride in Dad's taxi?

234
00:15:53,369 --> 00:15:55,746
Dad's taxi is a Mercedes.

235
00:15:55,829 --> 00:15:56,789
A Mercedes.

236
00:15:56,872 --> 00:15:58,916
Yeah, a 1991 Mercedes 300

237
00:15:58,999 --> 00:16:01,752
SEL. You know that by heart, too, right?

238
00:16:01,835 --> 00:16:05,798
So you're saying it's a 1991
Mercedes taxi.

239
00:16:06,674 --> 00:16:08,759
But do we even have taxis like that
in this country?

240
00:16:08,842 --> 00:16:10,052
You don't trust your dad?

241
00:16:10,135 --> 00:16:11,595
No, no, no.

242
00:16:12,554 --> 00:16:13,597
Then, could you perhaps...

243
00:16:13,681 --> 00:16:16,767
Could you tell me your exact destination?

244
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:19,186
If it's dangerous...

245
00:16:19,269 --> 00:16:22,147
you don't have to push yourself
to try.

246
00:16:22,231 --> 00:16:25,567
It's nearby, sir.

247
00:16:25,651 --> 00:16:28,445
Would it be all right if we stopped by
the PNB flagship store on the way?

248
00:16:28,529 --> 00:16:29,655
My daughter

249
00:16:29,738 --> 00:16:32,116
has always picked Choco Pies

250
00:16:32,199 --> 00:16:34,451
whenever I let her choose a snack,
even when she was little.

251
00:16:34,535 --> 00:16:35,369
Sure, let's do that.

252
00:16:35,452 --> 00:16:37,246
I might as well try one
while we're there.

253
00:16:37,329 --> 00:16:39,289
What makes them so special?

254
00:16:39,373 --> 00:16:41,542
Listen, sweetie.

255
00:16:41,625 --> 00:16:44,670
Dad's bringing you Choco Pies from PNB.

256
00:16:44,753 --> 00:16:47,047
Once you try their Choco Pies,

257
00:16:47,131 --> 00:16:48,966
you won't be able to eat the ones
from the supermarket again.

258
00:16:49,049 --> 00:16:51,385
Code Zero declared.
All available personnel, respond.

259
00:16:51,468 --> 00:16:54,555
A 1991 Mercedes-Benz 300 SEL,

260
00:16:54,638 --> 00:16:58,434
is currently headed to the PNB Pungnyeon
Bakery flagship store in Jeonju.

261
00:16:58,517 --> 00:16:59,351
Sweetie,

262
00:17:00,352 --> 00:17:01,687
you're all

263
00:17:01,770 --> 00:17:04,064
your dad has. You know that, right?

264
00:17:05,024 --> 00:17:07,026
After we lost your mom,

265
00:17:07,901 --> 00:17:11,113
I'm so grateful you grew up
so strong.

266
00:17:11,196 --> 00:17:12,531
That's more than enough for me.

267
00:17:12,614 --> 00:17:15,826
I don't expect anything from you.

268
00:17:16,660 --> 00:17:17,870
Just one thing.

269
00:17:18,579 --> 00:17:20,789
You know you can never
abandon Dad, right?

270
00:17:22,082 --> 00:17:23,917
You have to take care of Dad, okay?

271
00:17:24,793 --> 00:17:26,295
Don't forget Dad's all alone.

272
00:17:26,378 --> 00:17:27,337
- Sir.
- Don't forget.

273
00:17:27,421 --> 00:17:29,381
Our team is on the way now.

274
00:17:29,465 --> 00:17:31,050
You don't need to worry so much now.

275
00:17:31,717 --> 00:17:33,218
And...

276
00:17:33,302 --> 00:17:35,012
I think you should say less.

277
00:17:35,095 --> 00:17:36,722
Unnecessary talking could actually
put you in danger.

278
00:17:36,805 --> 00:17:38,557
Okay, I understand.

279
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:40,726
It's hard having to talk to Dad
for so long, isn't it?

280
00:17:40,809 --> 00:17:42,227
I'll let you go now!

281
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:43,812
No.
Please stay on the line.

282
00:17:45,689 --> 00:17:46,523
Hello?

283
00:17:47,274 --> 00:17:48,108
Hello?

284
00:17:58,202 --> 00:18:01,747
You're putting too much
pressure on your daughter,

285
00:18:01,830 --> 00:18:05,334
so she might find it harder

286
00:18:05,417 --> 00:18:07,628
to talk to her dad, don't you think?

287
00:18:08,629 --> 00:18:11,548
Yes, it's really hard.

288
00:18:11,632 --> 00:18:14,885
Still, wouldn't everything be okay
if you brought her Choco Pies?

289
00:18:16,011 --> 00:18:17,638
Are Choco Pies really that powerful?

290
00:18:25,521 --> 00:18:26,563
I ran a search on the vehicle,

291
00:18:26,647 --> 00:18:29,149
and there's only one 1991 Mercedes
taxi in the entire country.

292
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:30,734
It's so distinctive,

293
00:18:30,818 --> 00:18:32,236
the Jeonju operations center
spotted it right away.

294
00:18:32,319 --> 00:18:33,195
Really?

295
00:18:33,278 --> 00:18:35,823
But based on their location,
the taxi will get there

296
00:18:35,906 --> 00:18:37,783
about five minutes before we do.

297
00:18:37,866 --> 00:18:40,994
Right. Just hold on for five minutes.

298
00:18:41,078 --> 00:18:42,287
I hope so.

299
00:18:42,371 --> 00:18:44,123
Please.

300
00:18:57,427 --> 00:18:59,763
The line is so long.

301
00:18:59,847 --> 00:19:01,515
This won't work. Let's just go.

302
00:19:01,598 --> 00:19:02,933
Damn, we got here too early.

303
00:19:04,643 --> 00:19:06,687
Didn't we get here too late?

304
00:19:07,604 --> 00:19:09,314
The line's only going to get longer.

305
00:19:09,898 --> 00:19:12,401
Right, yes.

306
00:19:12,985 --> 00:19:14,236
It's a shame, but should we just go?

307
00:19:14,319 --> 00:19:16,238
I don't think we have time to wait.

308
00:19:16,321 --> 00:19:19,116
That's the line for Choco Pies.

309
00:19:19,199 --> 00:19:21,160
You can skip the line if
you buy something else.

310
00:19:22,536 --> 00:19:25,289
But you said your daughter
only eats Choco Pies...

311
00:19:27,541 --> 00:19:28,792
She needs to learn

312
00:19:28,876 --> 00:19:32,629
that the world doesn't always go her way.

313
00:19:42,806 --> 00:19:44,183
Yes.

314
00:19:44,266 --> 00:19:46,476
Go ahead and pick something.

315
00:19:52,691 --> 00:19:54,109
What's the point of this?

316
00:20:02,117 --> 00:20:03,160
You knew,

317
00:20:03,243 --> 00:20:05,662
didn't you, that the line
for Choco Pies would be long?

318
00:20:06,580 --> 00:20:09,708
How could I know without even looking...

319
00:20:09,791 --> 00:20:11,710
No, no. The line here is always long.

320
00:20:11,793 --> 00:20:13,962
It'll stay long, too.

321
00:20:14,046 --> 00:20:17,424
At places like this,
waiting in line is just the default.

322
00:20:17,507 --> 00:20:20,135
You knew the line would be long

323
00:20:20,219 --> 00:20:21,511
and came here anyway.

324
00:20:22,471 --> 00:20:24,973
Even if the line was long,

325
00:20:25,057 --> 00:20:27,851
I knew you'd be willing to wait.

326
00:20:27,935 --> 00:20:30,145
No, I hate
standing in line more than anything.

327
00:20:30,229 --> 00:20:31,939
That's why I said we should just go.

328
00:20:35,817 --> 00:20:38,278
I treated you too much like my daughter

329
00:20:38,362 --> 00:20:40,614
and put you on the spot,
like you were a customer. Yes.

330
00:20:40,697 --> 00:20:42,407
Your daughter choosing

331
00:20:42,491 --> 00:20:44,952
some lousy streusel bun instead of a
Choco Pie isn't going to suddenly make her

332
00:20:45,035 --> 00:20:47,579
'realize she can't live her life
exactly as she wants.'

333
00:20:47,663 --> 00:20:49,081
Do you really think she'd say that?

334
00:20:49,164 --> 00:20:50,540
Actually, the world

335
00:20:50,624 --> 00:20:54,169
doesn't work the way you think it does.

336
00:20:54,253 --> 00:20:56,296
I just thought

337
00:20:58,215 --> 00:21:01,760
maybe we were getting too caught up
in the herd mentality

338
00:21:01,843 --> 00:21:04,721
and making too big a deal
out of Choco Pies.

339
00:21:04,805 --> 00:21:07,766
You were the one making a fuss.

340
00:21:07,849 --> 00:21:09,101
You could just not buy one.

341
00:21:09,184 --> 00:21:11,353
Why buy this pointless bread?

342
00:21:12,396 --> 00:21:14,773
And ever since we got here,

343
00:21:15,691 --> 00:21:18,527
have you noticed your
attitude has changed?

344
00:21:20,988 --> 00:21:21,989
Something

345
00:21:22,823 --> 00:21:24,032
isn't right.

346
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:34,334
Where'd he go?

347
00:22:04,823 --> 00:22:06,533
You're the taxi driver
who filed the report, right?

348
00:22:06,616 --> 00:22:07,826
Yes.

349
00:22:07,909 --> 00:22:10,245
But we lost the suspect.

350
00:22:10,329 --> 00:22:11,955
I think he caught on at the last minute.

351
00:22:12,039 --> 00:22:13,749
We got here as fast as we could,

352
00:22:13,832 --> 00:22:15,459
but traffic was bad.

353
00:22:16,084 --> 00:22:18,170
Leave it to us from here.

354
00:22:18,253 --> 00:22:19,504
He can't have gotten far.

355
00:22:19,588 --> 00:22:20,422
Yes.

356
00:22:20,505 --> 00:22:21,673
Hey, you bastard.
I don't believe you, huh?

357
00:22:21,757 --> 00:22:23,467
- You crazy bastard, huh?
- Let go!

358
00:22:23,550 --> 00:22:24,676
I'm reporting you.

359
00:22:25,927 --> 00:22:27,054
How'd the police know
and get here ahead of time?

360
00:22:27,137 --> 00:22:28,722
Officer!

361
00:22:28,805 --> 00:22:29,806
Come over here!

362
00:22:30,932 --> 00:22:32,392
This guy

363
00:22:32,476 --> 00:22:34,519
pretended to buy another kind of bread
and skipped the line,

364
00:22:34,603 --> 00:22:36,938
then snuck right into our Choco Pie line.

365
00:22:37,022 --> 00:22:37,981
I saw the whole thing!

366
00:22:38,065 --> 00:22:39,191
Should I stomp him to death?

367
00:22:39,274 --> 00:22:41,068
You rat!
You little bastard!

368
00:22:41,151 --> 00:22:43,528
Can't you see that line over there?
Huh?

369
00:22:43,612 --> 00:22:44,905
You rat!

370
00:22:44,988 --> 00:22:45,947
Take him away!

371
00:22:56,458 --> 00:22:57,959
He was already wanted as a cash
courier for a phone scam ring.

372
00:22:58,043 --> 00:23:00,253
His name was on the wanted list.

373
00:23:01,630 --> 00:23:03,673
Then that paper bag...

374
00:23:05,258 --> 00:23:07,344
Luckily, the full amount
reported by both victims

375
00:23:07,427 --> 00:23:08,303
was in the paper bag.

376
00:23:09,096 --> 00:23:11,932
Thanks to you, we were able to
return it safely to the victims.

377
00:23:12,015 --> 00:23:14,059
I didn't do anything, really.

378
00:23:16,478 --> 00:23:17,604
Your daughter

379
00:23:17,687 --> 00:23:19,898
got you into this because you were
trying to buy her a Choco Pie.

380
00:23:22,442 --> 00:23:24,653
I'm sorry, but

381
00:23:24,736 --> 00:23:26,321
I'm not even married

382
00:23:26,404 --> 00:23:27,864
and I don't have any kids.

383
00:23:28,573 --> 00:23:30,700
Hey, you bastard!
You son of a bitch!

384
00:23:31,827 --> 00:23:32,953
You bastard!

385
00:23:46,758 --> 00:23:48,927
Funny thing is,

386
00:23:49,010 --> 00:23:51,138
I never get my fare when I come to Jeonju.

387
00:23:57,102 --> 00:23:59,020
Mister!

388
00:23:59,104 --> 00:24:00,939
Mister!

389
00:24:02,023 --> 00:24:03,316
Mister!

390
00:24:03,400 --> 00:24:05,318
We finally run into each other here!

391
00:24:05,402 --> 00:24:07,362
Mister, I didn't run off that day.

392
00:24:07,445 --> 00:24:09,447
I have really bad anemia.

393
00:24:09,531 --> 00:24:12,909
I suddenly collapsed inside the ATM booth.

394
00:24:12,993 --> 00:24:14,661
I almost died that day. Seriously.

395
00:24:14,744 --> 00:24:16,496
They found me too late.

396
00:24:16,580 --> 00:24:17,706
Mister, look at this.

397
00:24:18,498 --> 00:24:19,875
I'm serious!

398
00:24:19,958 --> 00:24:21,042
I had to get stitches in my head.

399
00:24:21,126 --> 00:24:23,086
I came straight here after
getting my head stitched up,

400
00:24:23,170 --> 00:24:25,338
but that night,
there wasn't a taxi in sight.

401
00:24:25,422 --> 00:24:26,631
It was so scary being out at night,

402
00:24:26,715 --> 00:24:28,633
and I felt so, so bad.

403
00:24:28,717 --> 00:24:30,468
- You can actually transfer the money here, too.
- I...

404
00:24:30,552 --> 00:24:32,554
Th-this, in your mouth...

405
00:24:32,637 --> 00:24:35,098
- In your mouth, yes, that...
- This? This one?

406
00:24:37,100 --> 00:24:38,268
Right, I...

407
00:24:38,351 --> 00:24:40,812
I'll transfer the taxi
fare I owed you right away.

408
00:24:40,896 --> 00:24:42,189
Okay.

409
00:24:43,190 --> 00:24:44,816
Mister, this is a gift for you.

410
00:24:44,900 --> 00:24:47,319
Please, have lots of
it when you get inside.

411
00:24:47,402 --> 00:24:48,361
Okay.

412
00:24:48,445 --> 00:24:50,030
- I should get going.
- Yes, yes, yes.

413
00:24:50,113 --> 00:24:52,073
Take care getting home, sir.

414
00:24:52,157 --> 00:24:53,366
- Bye! See you again.
- Yes.

415
00:24:58,663 --> 00:25:02,209
♪ You said you'd come back ♪

416
00:25:03,835 --> 00:25:07,839
♪ You said it would
only be a little while ♪

417
00:25:09,507 --> 00:25:13,553
♪ You told me to wait here ♪

418
00:25:13,637 --> 00:25:17,557
♪ Lies, lies, lies ♪

419
00:25:20,352 --> 00:25:24,147
♪ I stood there staring
as the sun went down ♪

420
00:25:25,982 --> 00:25:29,736
♪ I curled up as the night wore on ♪

421
00:25:31,363 --> 00:25:35,367
♪ But in the end, you never showed up ♪

422
00:25:35,450 --> 00:25:39,704
♪ Lies, lies ♪

423
00:25:40,538 --> 00:25:45,335
♪ Only you ♪

424
00:25:46,670 --> 00:25:50,799
♪ I waited for you endlessly ♪

425
00:25:51,466 --> 00:25:56,221
♪ Your words ♪

426
00:25:57,639 --> 00:26:02,269
♪ I believed them with all my heart ♪

427
00:26:08,483 --> 00:26:13,154
♪ The road froze in the biting wind ♪

428
00:26:19,119 --> 00:26:23,623
♪ And I froze white as snow ♪

429
00:26:28,670 --> 00:26:32,215
♪ You said I hadn't done anything wrong ♪

430
00:26:34,092 --> 00:26:37,804
♪ You said I was a good person ♪

431
00:26:39,514 --> 00:26:43,643
♪ You said you'd embrace even my hurt ♪

432
00:26:43,727 --> 00:26:47,897
♪ Lies, lies ♪

433
00:26:50,400 --> 00:26:54,279
♪ Once again, I'm left all alone ♪

434
00:26:55,864 --> 00:26:59,826
♪ And all our memories get thrown away ♪

435
00:27:01,286 --> 00:27:05,415
♪ I guess I'm not worthy after all ♪

436
00:27:05,498 --> 00:27:09,377
♪ Lies ♪

437
00:27:10,503 --> 00:27:15,467
♪ Only you ♪

438
00:27:16,676 --> 00:27:20,847
♪ I waited for you endlessly ♪

439
00:27:21,514 --> 00:27:26,394
♪ Your words ♪

440
00:27:27,645 --> 00:27:32,317
♪ I believed them with all my heart ♪

441
00:27:38,490 --> 00:27:43,203
♪ The road froze in the biting wind ♪

442
00:27:49,084 --> 00:27:53,546
♪ And I froze white as snow ♪
